From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: visuals shared with another process (the desktop device's partner interface)

The WebView2 runtime asks the dcomp desktop device for an undocumented
partner interface ({d14b6158-c3fa-4bce-9c1f-b61d8665eab0}) when its host
composes it without a window of its own, as Office does for its task panes
(msAbydosForWindowlessWV2), and gave up on E_NOINTERFACE: Excel's Copilot
pane said "This feature could not be started". The host makes a visual and
a handle to it; the browser process opens a target on the handle and shows
its own window there through CreateSurfaceFromHwnd. The desktop device now
has the partner's three methods, and such a window goes into the host's
window, where its process keeps it.
---
